WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.853
This course is a loop, not a binge library.

00:00:02.853 --> 00:00:05.073
Watching alone does not count as finishing.

00:00:05.073 --> 00:00:07.609
This lesson is about the digprog weekly loop.

00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:10.463
Watch → quiz → one outreach → note learning.

00:00:10.463 --> 00:00:12.682
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:12.682 --> 00:00:15.853
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:15.853 --> 00:00:20.608
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:20.608 --> 00:00:24.096
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:24.416 --> 00:00:32.405
Each week has four steps: watch one lesson, take the quiz, do one real outreach or action, then note what you learned.

00:00:32.405 --> 00:00:35.311
Remember the objective: describe the weekly loop steps.

00:00:35.311 --> 00:00:39.305
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:43.663
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:43.663 --> 00:00:47.658
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.658 --> 00:00:52.016
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:52.336 --> 00:00:53.806
The quiz forces retrieval.

00:00:53.806 --> 00:00:56.011
The action forces contact with reality.

00:00:56.011 --> 00:00:58.217
The note captures the next move.

